        "abstract": "Electrostatic discharge (ESD) failure remains a major integrated circuit (IC) reliability challenge. Though devices being the foundational elements, on-chip ESD protection design is essentially a complex full-chip design task. A follow-up to a prior overview of device innovation in on-chip ESD protection, this paper reviews major ESD protection design innovation including various computer-aided design (CAD)-enabled ESD protection circuit design techniques and methodologies aiming for ESD protection design optimization and prediction, as well as advances in CAD tool and flow enabling full-chip ESD physical design verification.",
